-- title:
--   Local equality at q ∤ N of an Eichler order and a maximal order above it
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $q'$ in the sense of the project predicate: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and $N$ a natural number with $R$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_1'$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_1'$ with relative index $[\Lambda_1:R]=N$; here an order is a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated, and spanning $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and it is maximal when every order containing it equals it. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq q'$ and $q\nmid N$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $q$. Finally let $\Lambda_2$ be a maximal order with $R\subseteq\Lambda_2$. Then the two local boxes at $v$ agree: the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda_2$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$ equals the corresponding subgroup built from $R$.
--
--   This is the local statement that away from the level and from the ramified prime an Eichler order is already locally maximal, so that any maximal order containing it has the same completion; it rests on the fact that at a split prime the maximal orders of $M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ are the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$-conjugates of $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_v)$ and that no proper inclusion between two such conjugates occurs. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd tower, where Eichler orders obtained by intersecting with Hecke translates must be identified locally at primes not dividing the level.
-- source:
